import LeanExe.ProofKit.BesselLarge0
import LeanExe.ProofKit.BesselRatio

/-!
Short polynomials for comparing `P0` and `Q0` with fdlibm's rational approximations.  Each piece of
`BesselLarge0` splits into segments of dyadic width, and on each segment `[a, b]` a polynomial of
degree 16 in `x - c`, with `c` the segment's center and dyadic coefficients, lies within `2^-71` of
the piece's polynomials (`segOk`).  On `[30, ∞)`, Hankel's expansion truncated to degree 26 with
dyadic coefficients lies within `2^-72` of the 60-term expansion.  With the bounds of
`BesselLarge0`, `P0` and `Q0` lie within `2^-70` of these polynomials (`near_seg`, `near_asym`),
and the step lemmas combine this with a kernel check of `BesselRatio` on one segment.
-/

namespace LeanExe.ProofKit.BesselSeg0

open Set PolyBound PolyCalc BesselPQ BesselChain BesselRatio BesselLarge0

